#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# spheroidal_ps

#% text
# `spheroidal_ps(n, m, gamma, x)` gives the angular spheroidal function of the first kind `Ps^m_n(x, gamma^2)` for `-1 < x < 1`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The function is the sum `sum (-1)^k a_k P^m_(n+2k)(x)` of Ferrers functions (Condon-Shortley phase) with the coefficients of the eigenvalue's continued fraction (DLMF 30.8.1), normalized by `integrate(Ps^2, [x, -1, 1]) = 2 (n + m)!/((2n + 1)(n - m)!)` (DLMF 30.4.4).

#% item
# Integers `n >= m >= 0`; `spheroidal_ps(n, m, 0, x) = legendre_p(n, m, x)`; arguments with `|x| >= 1` stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
spheroidal_ps(5, 1, 0, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.16079837663884378

#% cell
n(spheroidal_ps(7, 5, 4, 0), 50)
#% output
#= 5197.949191793180304847731343835592982674520025655020852

#% cell
n(spheroidal_ps(2, 1, 1/3, 1/2), 20)
#% output
#= -1.300875733572396152328754

#% cell
spheroidal_ps(2, 0, 1.0, 0.3)
#% output
#= -0.34480205554972826

#% text
# The normalization:

#% cell
n_integrate(spheroidal_ps(2, 0, 1.5, x)^2, [x, -1, 1])
#% output
#= 0.3999999999999999

#% cell
n(2/5)
#% output
#= 0.4

